1. RESOURCE CHANGE REQUEST (6 endpoints)
-------------------------------------------
Full spec: BACKEND_RESOURCE_CHANGE_REQUEST_API.md (request/response JSON,
DB schema for 4 tables, error code matrix — all already written).

[ ] POST /api/admin/resource_change_requests
    Params: { status, priority, search, page, limit } — all optional filters
    Returns: list + summary counts (total/pending/approved/rejected) + pagination

[ ] POST /api/admin/resource_change_request_detail
    Params: { request_id }
    Returns: project + client info, current_allocation[], requested_allocation[],
    attachments[], payment_milestones[], activity_log[]

[ ] POST /api/admin/approve_resource_change
    Params: { request_id, pmo_id, pmo_remarks }
    Side effect: must apply the requested allocation to the project's live
    resource_allocations, not just flip a status flag

[ ] POST /api/admin/reject_resource_change
    Params: { request_id, pmo_id, rejection_reason }  (rejection_reason required)

[ ] POST /api/admin/clarify_resource_change
    Params: { request_id, pmo_id, clarification_query }

[ ] POST /api/projectManager/create_resource_change_request
    Params: (PM-side submission — not in api.js yet, needs adding once live)
    project_id, pm_id, requested_allocation[], reason_by_pm, pm_request_note,
    attachments[] (optional)


2. PROJECT REALLOCATION (1 endpoint)
-------------------------------------------
[ ] POST /api/admin/re-allocated
    Real frontend call site: src/pages/CreateProjectPage.jsx,
    handleConfirmAssignPM() — payload format is multipart/form-data, NOT JSON:
      id: <project_id>
      pm_id: <project_id>          <-- BUG, see below
      project_manager: <string, new PM's display name>
      status: "re-allocated"
    Returns: { success, message }

    ⚠️ KNOWN FRONTEND BUG (flag to backend before they build against this):
    pm_id is currently set to the PROJECT's id, not the new PM's actual
    user/resource id (copy-paste mistake in CreateProjectPage.jsx). Confirm
    the real intended field with frontend/backend together before locking
    this contract in — implementing it as-is will silently misassign PMs.


3. UPDATE PROJECT MILESTONE (1 endpoint)
-------------------------------------------
[ ] POST /api/projectManager/update_project_milestone
    STATUS: no frontend call site exists yet (endpoint is defined in
    api.js but never called) — shape below is INFERRED from the existing
    milestone schema, not confirmed. Treat as a proposal to align on.

    Suggested params:
      project_id: number
      milestone: string        (matches how milestones are created/read)
      milestone_date: "YYYY-MM-DD"
      percentage: number

    OPEN QUESTION — blocking a real contract: milestones have no stable
    `id` in the current read shape (get_projectList's milestones[] is just
    { milestone, percentage, milestone_date }, no id). A project can have
    two milestones with the same name (e.g. two "Sign-off" phases) — so
    "update by name" is ambiguous. RECOMMEND backend add a milestone_id
    column, return it in get_projectList's milestones[], and require it
    here — matching how every other update endpoint in this app (e.g.
    UPDATE_BOARD) keys off a real row id, not a name match.


